From 8a5a015efcd010f472e29113b0505f30cad515a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 04:57:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] corpus integrity: gen.sh + fnv1a64 checksums + load-time
 verification

the 4ad2cbd lesson: the landing medium replaced the invalid-utf-8 seed's
bytes with U+FFFD, silently flipping its crosscheck verdict from reject
to accept - the first drift in five landings, and the corpus became an
integrity-critical input the moment the fuzzer committed it.

- tests/fuzz/corpus/gen.sh: the binary seeds regenerate from pure-ascii
  octal escapes (idempotent healer; the escapes are the source of truth,
  the committed bytes the cache - the medium never gets the last word)
- tests/fuzz/corpus/checksums: fnv1a64 pin per seed, committed
- okfuzz --checksums <dir>: the regen lane; both consuming lanes (fuzz +
  crosscheck) verify the pins at corpus load - a moved seed, an unpinned
  seed, or a pin naming a missing seed all fail loudly naming the file,
  with the gen.sh/crosscheck.sh command that settles it
- crosscheck.sh: gen.sh heals before anything walks, then manifest and
  pins regenerate together - one regen door
- the manifest catches up the 8 repl fixtures patch 60 shipped
  unregistered (found by this lane's own regen: 4 intentional rejects,
  the continuation-shaped entries)

gates: builds 9/9, e2e 603x7, unit+embed 5x3, capi 334x5, cli 10/10,
fuzz x2 byte-identical (47702 diagnostics, 0 unlocated), delta flat
(1.40654e7, 1.93x/1.87x)
